{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>From the children of Israel.</b> It may be explained along the lines of what they said in the Tosefta of Shekalim (Tosefta Shekalim 2): all public offerings that were donated voluntarily are valid, provided that they hand them over to the public — thus far is their language. And this is what the verse means by <b>from the children of Israel</b>: namely, that this oil is a public offering, and therefore even if an individual were to donate it, he must hand it over to the public, and its bringing to the Tabernacle would be from the children of Israel."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:33:52.095390497Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}